Zugfolge license notice
========================

Zugfolge uses a component-specific license matrix. No single license applies to
every file in this repository.

The authoritative file-level assignment is `REUSE.toml`:

- original program code, tests, build and runtime configuration are licensed
  under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later
  (`AGPL-3.0-or-later`);
- public OpenAPI, AsyncAPI, JSON Schema contracts, contract examples, and
  generated public SDKs are licensed under the Apache License 2.0
  (`Apache-2.0`);
- original specifications, architecture decisions, plans, and documentation
  are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  (`CC-BY-4.0`), attributed to Zugfolge contributors;
- a future OSM-derived database release may be distributed under the Open Data
  Commons Open Database License 1.0 (`ODbL-1.0`) only when that release carries
  its own approval, attribution, provenance, and database-offer notice. No
  current database artifact is licensed merely because that future policy is
  documented here.
- provenance-pending fixtures and media explicitly mapped to
  `LicenseRef-Zugfolge-Provenance-Pending` are excluded from the license grants
  above until they are replaced, removed, or approved under a standard
  license.

Complete texts for licenses currently assigned to repository files are stored
in `LICENSES/`. ODbL remains a future policy only; its official text is linked
from `docs/LICENSING.md` and will be added with the first approved database
artifact.

Third-party dependencies, imported data, fonts, and separately identified
media retain their own licenses or contractual terms. Any later copyright
license for a cleared Block-Z rendering grants no permission to imply
endorsement and grants no trademark rights in the name Zugfolge, the Block-Z
designation, or other source identifiers. See `TRADEMARKS.md`.

Copyright notices and file assignments follow the REUSE Specification. If a
file-level SPDX notice conflicts with this summary, the file-level notice and
`REUSE.toml` control.
